      ],
      "answer": "The customer's issue that started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. They experienced search relevance degradation and increased manual triage time due to the taxonomy change on 2026-02-20, as documented in the support ticket and retro analysis. The root cause was linked to the taxonomy rollout date, involving outdated index weighting and schema registry version mismatches.\n\nThe proof plan proposed to BlueHarbor Logistics to get them comfortable with renewal includes:\n\n- A short-term mitigation involving updating index weighting and adding a translation/mapping layer for the top 20 saved searches.\n- Receiving schema registry export and query logs by 2026-03-19.\n- Starting an A/B test in staging on 2026-03-22 lasting 7-10 business days.\n- Acceptance criteria: top-5 correct hit rate \u2265 80%, no regression in suppression logic, and incident correlation latency < 200ms.\n- If successful, a 1-day production rollout and 72-hour monitoring follow.\n- Offering a 90-day professional services engagement at $48k fixed price, with a 30% discount if Orchestrator seat expansion is signed concurrently.\n- Including a conditional credit clause if the proof does not meet the agreed metrics within 10 business days.\n\nThis detailed proof plan is documented in the renewal negotiation call and retro artifacts.\n\nNo other customer's issue starting after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout or proof plan details for other customers are identified in the evidence. [art_8b0063fbb3cb, art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194, art_c9970c1dc932]",
