      "answer": "In the MapleHarvest Quebec pilot, the temporary field mappings planned in the router transform include mapping txn_id to transaction_id, total_amount to amount_cents, performing type coercion from string to int, preserving key fields store_id and register_id, and adding a transformation flag field _ns_transform=true. This transform is deployed in SI-CLOUD-ROUTER as a temporary measure to address SI-SCHEMA-REG rejections caused by mixed field names and types from store-level preprocessing. Additionally, the transform enables OR-AUDIT-LOGS for each transformed event to support audit purposes [art_5a91258f4056].\n\nThe March 23 workshop in the MapleHarvest Quebec pilot is a Schema Signoff Workshop with the agenda to agree on a canonical schema for payment, register_events, and sensor_thermo; define alias mapping; and establish a producer migration plan. The deliverable from this workshop is a signed schema document to be uploaded to SI-SCHEMA-REG and a change control ticket that includes producer migration milestones [art_5a91258f4056].\n\nNo further details on additional temporary field mappings beyond those specified or on the exact outputs or format of the March 23 workshop deliverables beyond the signed schema document and change control ticket are provided in the evidence.",
