      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is Pioneer Freight Solutions. They are currently running a tactical proof of concept (PoC) of NoiseGuard, a lower-priced tactical noise reduction competitor. The exact milestone at risk is the acceptance milestone for the remediation plan addressing the taxonomy change incident. This milestone is the validation window acceptance criteria due by 2026-05-14, which requires achieving precision@10 of at least 0.8 for facility lookups, an entity-link hit rate of at least 90%, and grouping false positives of 5% or less. The remediation plan includes schema registry verification by 2026-03-22, shadow index build from 2026-03-29 to 2026-04-09, backfill and index weight recomputation from 2026-04-12 to 2026-04-30, and the validation window from 2026-05-01 to 2026-05-14. There is also a commercial offer of a one-time credit equal to 10% of annual contract value ($42,000) if the milestone acceptance is not met by the agreed dates, underscoring the criticality of meeting these milestones to prevent defection to NoiseGuard. NoiseGuard is seen as a cheaper, tactical alternative that addresses symptom-level alert noise but lacks deeper schema registry awareness and automation, making it attractive for immediate tactical needs but less effective long-term compared to Northstar's full remediation plan. The risk of defection is high if Northstar misses acceptance milestones, as procurement is likely to extend NoiseGuard usage and reduce Northstar's scope, fragmenting the stack [art_7373b64fdfdd, art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_79cf94421871, art_e2727db588de].\n\nNo other customers besides Pioneer Freight Solutions are explicitly identified as likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if milestones are missed, and no exact milestone details for other customers or competitors besides Pioneer Freight Solutions and NoiseGuard are provided. Quantitative likelihood or scoring of defection risk beyond qualitative assessment for Pioneer Freight Solutions is also not available in the evidence.",
